# Path: .env.example
# Purpose: Documentation of the inert `VITE_` variables the application reads, with no secrets
# Lines: 23
#
# These values are placeholders, not credentials. Copy this file to `.env` to change either one
# locally: `.env` is git-ignored, this file is committed, and nothing here is required to run.
#
# Only VITE_-prefixed names reach client code, because Vite replaces import.meta.env.VITE_* at
# build time and exposes nothing else; an unprefixed variable here would silently do nothing.
#
# The application runs identically with no `.env` file at all: this file sets nothing by itself, and
# each variable's in-code default lives in the module that reads it. No secret, key or token belongs
# in this file, in `.env`, or anywhere else in the tree.
#
# Product name. No module reads this variable today: the name the application renders (the header
# brand, the footer line and every page title, through documentTitle) comes from APP_COPY.APP_NAME
# in src/constants/content.ts, and the document title index.html declares is a literal.
VITE_APP_NAME=SalesPro
# Simulated latency in ms (default 120). The reader is src/lib/mockServer.ts, which falls back to
# DEFAULT_API_LATENCY_MS in src/constants/config.ts for a value it cannot apply, and
# src/lib/apiClient.ts waits it out once before every mock-server response. Tests pin it to 0 in
# code, so lowering it here only speeds the dev server up.
VITE_API_LATENCY_MS=120
